    {
      "name": "OcsfAgent",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAgent",
      "instantiates": [
        "ocsf:OcsfFacts"
      ],
      "annotations": [
        {
          "tag": "ocsf_key",
          "value": "agent",
          "@type": "Annotation"
        },
        {
          "tag": "ocsf_constraints",
          "value": "{\"at_least_one\": [\"uid\", \"name\"]}",
          "@type": "Annotation"
        }
      ],
      "description": "An Agent (also known as a Sensor) is typically installed on an Operating System (OS) and serves as a specialized software component that can be designed to monitor, detect, collect, archive, or take action. These activities and possible actions are defined by the upstream system controlling the Agent and its intended purpose. For instance, an Agent can include Endpoint Detection & Response (EDR) agents, backup/disaster recovery sensors, Application Performance Monitoring or profiling sensors, and similar software.",
      "title": "Agent",
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/ocsf_objects",
      "see_also": [
        "https://d3fend.mitre.org/dao/artifact/d3f:Sensor/"
      ],
      "exact_mappings": [
        "ocsf:OcsfAgent"
      ],
      "related_mappings": [
        "d3f:Sensor"
      ],
      "is_a": "OcsfObjectBase",
      "slots": [
        "OcsfAgent_name",
        "OcsfAgent_policies",
        "OcsfAgent_type",
        "OcsfAgent_type_id",
        "OcsfAgent_uid",
        "OcsfAgent_uid_alt",
        "OcsfAgent_vendor_name",
        "OcsfAgent_version"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAgent",
      "any_of": [
        {
          "slot_conditions": [
            {
              "name": "uid",
              "required": true,
              "@type": "SlotDefinition"
            }
          ],
          "@type": "AnonymousClassExpression"
        },
        {
          "slot_conditions": [
            {
              "name": "name",
              "required": true,
              "@type": "SlotDefinition"
            }
          ],
          "@type": "AnonymousClassExpression"
        }
      ],
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "OcsfAiAgent",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAiAgent",
      "instantiates": [
        "ocsf:OcsfFacts"
      ],
      "annotations": [
        {
          "tag": "ocsf_key",
          "value": "ai_agent",
          "@type": "Annotation"
        },
        {
          "tag": "ocsf_profiles",
          "value": "container data_classification",
          "@type": "Annotation"
        },
        {
          "tag": "ocsf_constraints",
          "value": "{\"at_least_one\": [\"name\", \"uid\"]}",
          "@type": "Annotation"
        }
      ],
      "description": "An autonomous AI agent that performs tasks under delegated authority. Distinguished from the OCSF agent object (which describes security sensors such as EDR and DLP tools) and from human principals. An AI agent has a stable logical identity across runs and a restart-sensitive instance identity. The agent owns its model; the ai_model attribute captures which model was backing the agent at the time of action.",
      "title": "AI Agent",
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/ocsf_objects",
      "exact_mappings": [
        "ocsf:OcsfAiAgent"
      ],
