    {
      "name": "OcsfToken",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfToken",
      "instantiates": [
        "ocsf:OcsfFacts"
      ],
      "annotations": [
        {
          "tag": "ocsf_key",
          "value": "token",
          "@type": "Annotation"
        },
        {
          "tag": "ocsf_profiles",
          "value": "datetime",
          "@type": "Annotation"
        }
      ],
      "description": "The Token object is the base object for representing tokens, API keys, and authentication credentials used across different contexts. This object provides common attributes for all token types, including protocol-specific authentication tokens (Kerberos, OIDC, SAML) and API/client tokens used for service authentication. When to use this object: Use the base <code>token</code> object directly in API activity events to represent API tokens, client tokens, or API keys used to authenticate API requests. Examples include: Okta API tokens, Microsoft Entra ID Application Registration client secrets, Stripe API keys, AWS API keys. When NOT to use this object: Do NOT use the base <code>token</code> object for protocol-specific authentication tokens in authentication events - use <code>authentication_token</code> instead (which extends this object). Do NOT use <code>token</code> for tracking credential lifecycle and usage patterns - use <code>programmatic_credential</code> instead.",
      "title": "Token",
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/ocsf_objects",
      "exact_mappings": [
        "ocsf:OcsfToken"
      ],
      "is_a": "OcsfObjectBase",
      "slots": [
        "OcsfToken_created_time",
        "OcsfToken_created_time_dt",
        "OcsfToken_expiration_time",
        "OcsfToken_expiration_time_dt",
        "OcsfToken_is_renewable",
        "OcsfToken_modified_time",
        "OcsfToken_modified_time_dt",
        "OcsfToken_name",
        "OcsfToken_tenant_uid",
        "OcsfToken_type",
        "OcsfToken_type_id",
        "OcsfToken_uid",
        "OcsfToken_zone"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfToken",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "OcsfAuthenticationToken",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAuthenticationToken",
      "instantiates": [
        "ocsf:OcsfFacts"
      ],
      "annotations": [
        {
          "tag": "ocsf_key",
          "value": "authentication_token",
          "@type": "Annotation"
        },
        {
          "tag": "ocsf_profiles",
          "value": "datetime",
          "@type": "Annotation"
        }
      ],
      "description": "The Authentication Token object extends the base <code>token</code> object and represents standardized authentication tokens, tickets, or assertions that conform to established authentication protocols such as Kerberos, OIDC, and SAML. This object inherits all attributes from <code>token</code> and adds protocol-specific attributes (e.g., <code>kerberos_flags</code>, <code>encryption_details</code>) for authentication events. Use this object in authentication events to represent protocol-specific tokens: Kerberos Ticket Granting Tickets (TGT) and Service Tickets (ST), OIDC Identity Tokens and Refresh Tokens, and SAML Assertions. These tokens are issued by authentication servers and identity providers and carry protocol-specific metadata, lifecycle information, and security attributes defined by their respective specifications. When to use this object: Use <code>authentication_token</code> when representing protocol-specific authentication tokens (type_id values 1-5: Kerberos TGT/ST, OIDC ID/Refresh tokens, SAML assertions) in authentication events. When NOT to use this object: Do NOT use <code>authentication_token</code> for API tokens or client tokens (type_id values 6-7) used in API activity events - use the base <code>token</code> object instead. Do NOT use <code>authentication_token</code> for generic API keys - use the base <code>token</code> object instead.",
      "title": "Authentication Token",
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/ocsf_objects",
      "exact_mappings": [
        "ocsf:OcsfAuthenticationToken"
      ],
      "is_a": "OcsfToken",
      "slots": [
        "OcsfToken_modified_time",
        "OcsfToken_modified_time_dt",
        "OcsfToken_name",
        "OcsfToken_tenant_uid",
        "OcsfToken_uid",
        "OcsfToken_zone",
        "OcsfAuthenticationToken_encryption_details",
        "OcsfAuthenticationToken_kerberos_flags",
        "OcsfAuthenticationToken_created_time",
        "OcsfAuthenticationToken_created_time_dt",
        "OcsfAuthenticationToken_expiration_time",
        "OcsfAuthenticationToken_expiration_time_dt",
        "OcsfAuthenticationToken_is_renewable",
        "OcsfAuthenticationToken_type",
        "OcsfAuthenticationToken_type_id"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAuthenticationToken",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "OcsfAuthorization",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAuthorization",
      "instantiates": [
        "ocsf:OcsfFacts"
